[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"External Tool Integrations in Jenkins (Maven, Gradle, SonarQube, Nexus/Artifactory)"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Jenkins acts as the central orchestration engine for Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD). To build robust pipelines, Jenkins must integrate seamlessly with external tools for building, testing, quality analysis, and artifact management."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Configuring Global Tools (Maven and Gradle)"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To compile Java projects, Jenkins needs access to build tools like Apache Maven or Gradle. You can configure these globally so they are available across all Jenkins agents."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Navigate to Manage Jenkins -> Tools in your Jenkins dashboard."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Locate the Maven section and click Add Maven."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Provide a name (e.g., 'Maven-3.8.x') and either check 'Install automatically' to let Jenkins download it or provide the path to a pre-installed home directory."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Repeat a similar configuration for Gradle under the Gradle section."},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Integrating SonarQube for Code Quality"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"SonarQube performs static code analysis to detect bugs, vulnerabilities, and code smells. Integrating it requires the SonarQube Scanner plugin."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Install the 'SonarQube Scanner' plugin via Manage Jenkins -> Plugins."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Generate a user token in your SonarQube server dashboard and add it to Jenkins Credentials as a 'Secret text'."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Go to Manage Jenkins -> System, locate the SonarQube servers section, and add your server URL and credential ID."},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Integrating Nexus or Artifactory for Artifact Management"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once build and test phases succeed, binaries must be published to a repository manager like Nexus Repository or JFrog Artifactory."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Install the respective plugin (e.g., 'Nexus Artifact Uploader' or 'JFrog plugin')."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Configure server credentials securely in Manage Jenkins -> Credentials."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Reference the server IDs directly inside your declarative pipeline scripts."},{"order":19,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Pipeline Implementation Example"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"Below is a complete declarative Jenkinsfile demonstrating how to use Maven, SonarQube, and Nexus within a single pipeline."},{"order":21,"type":"code","text":"pipeline {
    agent any
    tools {
        maven 'Maven-3.8.x'
    }
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                checkout scm
            }
        }
        stage('Build and Test') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn clean package'
            }
        }
        stage('SonarQube Analysis') {
            steps {
                withSonarQubeEnv('MySonarServer') {
                    sh 'mvn sonar:sonar'
                }
            }
        }
        stage('Publish to Nexus') {
            steps {
                nexusPublisher(
                    nexusUrl: 'http://nexus.local:8081',
                    nexusVersion: 'nexus3',
                    protocol: 'http',
                    repositoryName: 'maven-releases',
                    credentialsId: 'nexus-credentials',
                    artifacts: [[artifactId: 'my-app', classifier: '', file: 'target/my-app.jar', type: 'jar']]
                )
            }
        }
    }
}"},{"order":22,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":23,"type":"paragraph","text":"By properly configuring global tools and leveraging plugins for SonarQube and Nexus/Artifactory, Jenkins transforms into a powerful automation server capable of enforcing strict quality gates and managing enterprise-grade software artifacts."}]
